<title>AUSTRALIA: CRICKET-SHEFFIELD SHIELD SCORES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SHEFFIELD SHIELD SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the</p>
<p>second day of Sheffield Shield matches played on Saturday:</p>
<p>In Perth: Western Australia beat New South Wales by nine</p>
<p>wickets.</p>
<p>Scores - New South Wales 89 (Bret Mulder five for two) and</p>
<p>217 (Bret Mulder six for 65); Western Australia 228 (Adam</p>
<p>Gilchrist 66) and 80 for one.</p>
<p>In Adelaide: South Australia 216 and 162 for two (Darren</p>
<p>Lehmann 70 not out); Victoria 241 (Ian Harvey 73)</p>
<p>In Hobart: Tasmania 408 (Ricky Ponting 159); Queensland 215</p>
<p>for five (Matthew Mott 74)</p>
</text>
